                                           set to 0 if command completed\n119\t\t                                             successfully */\n120\t\n121\t/**\n122\t * Parses the command line of a program\n123\t * and returns the number of non-options\n124\t * returned to the `extras' pointer (see\n125\t * below)\n126\t */\n127\tint\n128\txopt_parse(\n129\t\txoptContext             *ctx,             /* previously created XOpt context */\n130\t\tint                     argc,             /* argc, from int main() */\n131\t\tconst char              **argv,           /* argv, from int main() */\n132\t\tvoid                    *data,            /* a custom data object whos type\n133\t\t                                             corresponds to `.offset' values\n134\t\t                                             specified in the options list;\n135\t\t                                             populated with values interpreted\n136\t\t                                             from the command line */\n137\t\tconst char              ***extras,        /* receives a list of extra non-option\n138\t\t                                             arguments (i.e. files, subcommands,\n139\t\t                                             etc.) - length of which is returned\n140\t\t                                             by the function call */\n141\t\tconst char              **err);           /* pointer to a const char* that\n142\t\t                                             receives an err should one occur -\n143\t\t                                             set to 0 if command completed\n144\t\t                                             successfully */\n145\t\n146\t/**\n147\t * Generates and prints a help message\n148\t * and prints it to a FILE stream.\n149\t * If `defaults' is supplied, uses\n150\t * offsets (values) defined by the options\n151\t * list to show default options\n152\t */\n153\tvoid\n154\txopt_autohelp(\n155\t\txoptContext                 *ctx,    